[2.500209, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.502313, "o", "Create a terminal-based text editor. It should:\r\n\r\n- Open a file given as a command-line argument, or start with an empty buffer\r\n- Display the file contents with line numbers on the left\r\n- Show a status bar at the bottom with the filename, cursor position, and\r\n  whether the file has been modified\r\n- Support arrow keys for cursor movement\r\n- Support typing to insert characters at the cursor position\r\n- Support backspace and delete\r\n- Ctrl+S to save\r\n- Ctrl+Q to quit (warn if unsaved changes)\r\n- Page Up / Page Down for scrolling\r\n- Handle terminal resize\r\n\r\nUse raw terminal mode with termios. Don't use ncurses.\r\n"]
